  "interpretation": "<table style=\"width: 99.9535%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"><col style=\"width: 49.9303%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>NEGATIVE</td>\n<td>&nbsp;&lt; 12 U/ml</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>EQUIVOCAL</td>\n<td>&nbsp;12-18 U/ml</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POSITIVE</td>\n<td>&gt; 18 U/ml</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>COMMENTS:</strong><br>Anti-cardiolipin IgG/IgM is a solid phase enzyme immunoassay employing highly purified cardiolipin plus native human &beta;2-glycoprotein I for the quantitative and qualitative detection of IgG and/or IgM antibodies against cardiolipin in human serum. This assay is an aid in the&nbsp;diagnosis and risk estimation of thrombosis in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE).</p>",
